usage: flair [-h] [--version] [--log-stderr] [--log-level LOG_LEVEL]
             [--log-conf LOG_CONF] [--log-debug]
             <subcommand> ...

Run a FLAIR module. This program is the main entry point for running FLAIR
analysis.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             print FLAIR version
  --log-stderr          also log to stderr, even when logging to syslog
  --log-level LOG_LEVEL
                        Set level to integer or case-insensitive symbolic
                        value, one of: CRITICAL, FATAL, ERROR, WARN, WARNING,
                        INFO, DEBUG, NOTSET
  --log-conf LOG_CONF   Python logging configuration file, see
                        logging.config.fileConfig()
  --log-debug           short-cut that that sets --log-stderr and --log-
                        level=DEBUG

subcommands:
  <subcommand>
    align               Align reads to the genome
    transcriptome       Build a transcriptome from aligned reads
    quantify            Quantify isoform expression
    combine             Combine transcriptomes from multiple samples
    variantquant        Quantify variants at genome positions
    fusion              Identify gene fusions
    diffexp             Differential expression and usage analysis
    diffsplice          Call and test alternative splicing events
    alleles             Group reads into alleles from variants
    isoalleles          Group alleles by isoform
